    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (38 tests, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `contactPreference` field to the owner response that returns `EMAIL` when an email is present and `PHONE` otherwise.\n\n**1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `contactPreference` property to the `Owner` schema, typed as a string enum of `EMAIL` / `PHONE`. The OpenAPI generator turns this into an inner `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum`.\n\n**2. `src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that derives the value from the entity: `PHONE` when `getEmail()` is null/blank, `EMAIL` otherwise.\n\nThis is a purely derived response field (like the existing `displayName`, `membershipLevel`, `locality` mappings), so nothing needed to be stored on the entity or added to the OfficeFloor pipeline \u2014 the existing `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}` \u2192 `RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `OwnerMapper` path now includes it. Both new `Cp27Tests` cases (`PHONE` when no email, `EMAIL` when present) pass, and no existing tests regressed.",
